`more` with standard output that is not a terminal copies its input
whole, as POSIX and util-linux have it. Before, it still read keys
from the terminal to page through, so `zmore file.gz | cat`, or any
`more` in a script, waited forever. With several files, each starts
with util-linux's header naming it, and -s squeezes blank lines.

--- a/src/uu/more/src/more.rs
+++ b/src/uu/more/src/more.rs
